PART B – ONLINE SERVICES

This part applies when a Product offers online features (for example accounts, communities or virtual companies,
events, job boards, leaderboards, cloud sync, sharing or messaging – the "Online Services"). Online Services are
optional unless a schedule says a Product needs them.

10. Account
    10.1 To use Online Services you may need to sign in with a supported account (for example Discord or Steam)
         or create a Product account. You must be at least 16 years old, or have permission from a parent or
         guardian.
    10.2 Keep your account secure; you are responsible for what happens with it. Tell the Author without delay if
         you believe it was misused. One person, one account; accounts may not be sold, shared or transferred.

11. Your content
    11.1 "Your Content" is anything you create or upload through the Online Services (for example names,
         descriptions, logos, messages, events, jobs, images and uploaded data).
    11.2 You keep all rights in Your Content. You give the Author a free, worldwide, non-exclusive licence to store,
         process, display and share Your Content as far as needed to run, show and improve the Online Services.
         The licence ends when you delete Your Content or your account, except for copies in backups for a limited
         time and content others already shared with your permission.
    11.3 You confirm that you have the rights to Your Content and that it does not break the law or others' rights.

12. Conduct
    You may not use the Online Services to: a) harass, threaten, insult or discriminate against others, or post
    hateful, violent, sexual or illegal content; b) impersonate others or mislead about your identity; c) send spam
    or advertising; d) manipulate statistics, rankings or results (for example with fake data, cheats or
    automation); e) attack, overload, scan or reverse engineer the Online Services or use unofficial clients, bots
    or scrapers; f) collect other users' personal data.

13. Moderation, suspension and changes
    13.1 The Author may remove content, reset manipulated results, and warn, suspend or close accounts that break
         this agreement, the law or others' rights. Where reasonable you will be told why and can object.
    13.2 You can stop using the Online Services and delete your account at any time.
    13.3 The Author may change, pause or end Online Services or features, for example for maintenance, security or
         because a service is discontinued. Where possible this is announced in advance and you can export your
         data first. Paid services are covered by section 16.

14. Availability
    There is no guarantee that Online Services are always available, error-free or secure against all attacks.
    Local data in a Product is not affected by outages.


PART C – PAID FEATURES

This part applies only if the Author offers paid features for a Product (for example a one-time purchase,
subscription, supporter package, premium features, cosmetic items or donations with rewards – "Paid Features").
Nothing is ever charged without your separate, explicit agreement at the time of purchase.

15. Purchase and price
    15.1 The price, what is included, the term and how to cancel are shown before you buy. Prices include the
         statutory VAT where it applies.
    15.2 Payments are handled by the payment provider named at checkout under its own terms. The Author does not
         store your full payment details.
    15.3 Paid Features are licensed to you personally under this agreement; they are not sold as property and
         cannot be transferred or resold.

16. Subscriptions
    16.1 Subscriptions renew for the same term until you cancel. You can cancel at any time, at the latest before
         the next renewal, and keep access until the end of the paid term. The way to cancel is shown in the
         Product or on the Author's website.
    16.2 If a Paid Feature is discontinued during a paid term, you receive a pro-rata refund for the remaining time
         or an equivalent replacement.

17. Right of withdrawal (consumers in the EU/EEA/UK)
    17.1 As a consumer you can withdraw from a purchase within 14 days without giving a reason, as described in the
         withdrawal information shown at checkout.
    17.2 For digital content that is provided immediately, the right of withdrawal ends when the provision begins
         if you expressly agreed to the immediate start and confirmed that you know you lose the right of
         withdrawal. You will be asked for this at checkout.
    17.3 Statutory warranty rights for digital products (§§ 327 et seq. German Civil Code or the law of your
         country) remain unaffected.

18. Refunds and charge-backs
    Refunds are given as required by law and where the Author promises them. Charge-backs for purchases that were
    delivered as agreed may lead to the Paid Feature being disabled until the matter is resolved.


PART D – GENERAL

19. Warranty and liability
    19.1 Free Products and free features are provided "as is". For them, the Author gives no warranty that they are
         error-free or suitable for a particular purpose; make backups of important data.
    19.2 The Author is liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or
         health, under the German Product Liability Act and where a guarantee was given. For free Products, liability
         for simple negligence is excluded as far as the law allows (§§ 521, 599 German Civil Code). For Paid
         Features, liability for simple negligence is limited to the breach of essential contractual obligations and
         to the damage typical and foreseeable at the time of purchase.
    19.3 Mandatory rights you have as a consumer under the law of your country remain unaffected.

20. Termination
    This licence ends automatically if you seriously break this agreement; you must then uninstall the Product and
    delete all copies. Sections 2 to 5, 8, 11.2 (for content already shared), 19 and 22 continue to apply. Refunds
    for Paid Features follow Part C.

21. Changes to this agreement
    The Author may update this agreement, for example when new Products, features, Online Services or Paid Features
    are added. The current version is shown in the installer and inside each Product. For changes that matter to
    you, you will be asked to accept the new version when you install an update, sign in or buy something. Changes
    never reduce what you already paid for during its paid term.

22. Law and final provisions
    22.1 German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. If you
         are a consumer, this choice does not take away the protection of mandatory law of the country where you
         live.
    22.2 The EU online dispute resolution platform is available at https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr. The Author
         is not obliged and not willing to take part in dispute resolution proceedings before a consumer
         arbitration board, unless the law requires it.
    22.3 If a provision of this agreement is invalid, the rest remains valid.
    22.4 Each Product's Privacy Policy, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES and schedule are part of this agreement.

